From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SuperKali <hello@superkali.me>
Date: Thu, 14 May 2026 17:13:21 +0800
Subject: drm/msm/dp: Mark the link bad when an active sink is replugged

When the last connected DP/HDMI sink is unplugged, userspace may keep the
CRTC active while using a placeholder output. If the sink is plugged back
in later, the connector becomes connected again, but userspace might not
perform a full disable/enable modeset because the output still appears to
be active.

In that case the HPD unplug path has already torn down the DP link, while
the KMS state still describes an active stream. Simply reporting the sink
as connected is not enough to restore video.

Mark the connector link-status as BAD when a previously unplugged sink is
plugged back in while the DP stream is still marked powered on. This asks
userspace to perform a normal modeset, which lets the atomic enable path
retrain the link and restart the stream instead of trying to recover the
link from the HPD thread.

This fixes single-display unplug/replug on Plasma Wayland, where the
connector was connected and enabled after replug but the monitor received
no signal.

Signed-off-by: Xilin Wu <sophon@radxa.com>

(cherry picked from commit eb3247f6f9a39dcb15cf4b1df6d4732b1489b410)
[SuperKali: backported to sc8280xp edge from radxa/kernel linux-7.0.11]
Signed-off-by: SuperKali <hello@superkali.me>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
@@ -393,12 +393,14 @@ static int msm_dp_hpd_plug_handle(struct msm_dp_display_private *dp)
 {
 	int ret;
 	struct platform_device *pdev = dp->msm_dp_display.pdev;
+	bool was_plugged;
 
 	drm_dbg_dp(dp->drm_dev, "Before, type=%d sink_count=%d\n",
 			dp->msm_dp_display.connector_type,
 			dp->link->sink_count);
 
 	guard(mutex)(&dp->plugged_lock);
+	was_plugged = dp->plugged;
 
 	ret = pm_runtime_resume_and_get(&pdev->dev);
 	if (ret) {
@@ -412,6 +414,10 @@ static int msm_dp_hpd_plug_handle(struct msm_dp_display_private *dp)
 
 	ret = msm_dp_display_process_hpd_high(dp);
 
+	if (!ret && dp->msm_dp_display.power_on && !was_plugged)
+		drm_connector_set_link_status_property(dp->msm_dp_display.connector,
+						       DRM_MODE_LINK_STATUS_BAD);
+
 	drm_dbg_dp(dp->drm_dev, "After, type=%d sink_count=%d\n",
 			dp->msm_dp_display.connector_type,
 			dp->link->sink_count);
